  "lessons": [
    "Original-first geometry reference separated foam from original blue/yellow paint; concept used only for flat white/cream strokes and cyan accents.",
    "Small4x artwork on a large padded canvas expanded during generation. An8x reference improved stroke treatment, but did not lock dimensions.10x references made canvas occupancy more predictable.",
    "Raw preview glow mostly belongs to hidden RGB/very-low alpha. Blue composites showed transparent gaps and no broad visible matte; numerical alpha inspection preceded any cleanup decision.",
    "Exact numeric placement prompts did not guarantee exact tips. Left0.098 still exceeded the canvas by0.128HDpx at frame005, so the single family scale was fixed at0.097 before final export. Shared whole-family scales0.097left/0.09right preserve relative generated phase size without per-frame bounds fitting, but require full-scene shoreline approval.",
    "Foam cores peak at alpha254, not255. Preserve and report near-opacity rather than claiming binary opaque alpha.",
    "These line-only replacements omit legacy opaque ocean erase paint. The new background restore compositor is required for clean translucent redraws; engine verification belongs to the composed pilot."
  ],
